            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for to seethe, then the Tamil for to mutter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: திகில்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "திகில் — tikil — \"terror; horror\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அந்தக் கதையைக் கேட்டு எனக்குத் திகிலாக இருந்தது. antak kataiyaik kēṭṭu eṉakkut tikilāka iruntatu. Hearing that story, I felt terrified."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With இரு: திகிலாக இருந்தது, it was terrifying. A horror film is a திகில் (tikil) படம்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "திகில் (tikil) is native Dravidian (DEDR 3202); Kota in the same entry has a verb for being thunderstruck."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
